1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:13,000
This is ENRG — open verification infrastructure
that makes physical-world data cryptographically provable.
Not a token project: we sell trust.

2
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:30,500
STEP 1 — On-chain config: minting is gated, required: true.
A proof can only be minted after TWO independent,
staked oracles confirm it.
Oracles are economically aligned.

3
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:44,000
STEP 2 — A real device proof.
Oracle #1 signs the canonical SHA-256 hash and votes on-chain.
Votes: 1 — not yet finalized.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:02,800
STEP 3 — Oracle #2, an independent operator,
votes the SAME hash.
Attestation FINALIZED: votes 2, conflict false.
Any contradictory vote would trigger slashing.

5
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:14,700
STEP 4 — Oracles earn rewards from the staking fund.
It's idempotent: the second run claims nothing.

6
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:29,000
The full loop is proven on devnet:
register → claim → activate → mint
through the quorum gate → reward.
Repos are public; everything is inspectable on-chain.
Thank you.
